So, OK, so now you have to relinquish your weapons to get inside. There was a thing that explains the so OK, Rebel's End is a panopticon, a prison configured in such a way that the activities of the prisoners can be closely monitored.
From a central location situated on the frigid, misty coast of the Sea of Moving Ice, the prison is a single story structure topped with battlements. Rising from the core of the Panopticon is the tower that holds the prison's administrative offices and guard barracks. Both the prison and the tower.
Are carved from a tall blade shaped rock that rises high above the sea cliffs. This rock, called the windbreak, shields the tower against the brutal winds that sweep down from the rugged glacier. One can approach Rebels End by land, sea or air. A pier allows prisoners to be taken from.
Ships up an elevator to the prison and a mooring dock at the top of the tower allows prisoners to be delivered by airship. Rebels then is controlled by the Lord's Alliance, a loose confederation of settlements whose current members include the cities of Baldur's Gate, Mirabar, Neverwinter, Silvery Moon, Waterdeep.
And Yattar, the towns of Amfell, Daggerford and Longsaddle, and the Dwarven stronghold of Mithril Hall. To be imprisoned in Rebel's End, one must have committed a serious crime against one or more of the member cities and been sentenced to a lengthy period of incarceration, typically a year or more.
Each member of the Lord's Alliance assigns one representative to Rebel's End, and together those representatives form a parole committee called the Absolution Council. Rarely are all 10 council members present since Rebel's End offers little in the way of comfort and amenities if the council needs a tie breaking vote.
Breaking vote to determine whether to commute a prisoner sentence. The prison warden, who is a neutral arbiter with no ties to any Lord's Alliance member, will cast the deciding vote. And so that is how it works. The prison is hewn from stone, so all of the walls and floors and everything are stone.
It has 20 foot high outer walls and a flat 20 foot high ceiling throughout. Doors and hatches are made of reinforced iron.
And the prison personnel can lock. They can lock and unlock them. A locked door is is too strong to be shouldered or kicked open, but you think by looking at it, it can probably be destroyed if it takes enough damage.
Heating. The spaces are magically heated. The temperature is a constant 20 degrees Celsius. The exterior is -18 or colder. You will be. You will have exposure.
If if you go outside, there's lighting, those continual flame spells I mentioned you can. I mean in certain rooms you can control it by saying lights and the prison has a Garrison of 75 guards. They work 8 hour shifts. 2/3 of the Garrison is off duty and resting.
